T03e: bounded EvoIR text/field/proof audit, 2026-09-28

Base: 703661d; EvoIR 1.9.114 / EvoMIR 0.50. This is an erratum and
verification repair, not a new executable capability or full T03 closure.

RED
  section9_completeness.rs instantiated only 52 of the 59 current Inst
  variants despite its exhaustive schema match. Asm, AsmGoto, BitOperation,
  BlockAddr, FrameAddress, ReturnAddress and VaAccess were absent. A new
  independent source-enum inventory test fails on that exact set.
  Call/IndirectCall argument marks were hidden by `..`; external records,
  relative relocations and nested assembly records lacked structural coverage.
  Two new main-grammar tests fail: approved const.f128 is missing, and the
  ptr.offset operand production is erroneously attached to ptr.from_int.

Repair and clause mapping
  Section 9 field sentinel: instantiate every current variant, including all
  five VaAccess variants, nondefault assembly outputs/inputs/edges, byval call
  marks, extern/declaration records and relative relocation metadata. Nested
  record destructuring is exhaustive. The manifest now checks 143/143 keys.
  The sentinel intentionally is not an executable validated module; it checks
  serialization fields, not instruction execution or arbitrary semantic values.
  Section 2.4 / operand traversal: ten added instruction representatives have
  independently listed operand/result IDs and checked operand remapping. The
  repeated tokens on mutually exclusive assembly edges remain repeated.
  Sections 8/11 / Appendix D byval varargs: a valid scalar proof preserves a
  va_arg record. Four independently mutated, well-typed canonical outputs have
  recomputed output digests; checker exit 3 rejects changed HFA element/count,
  erased HFA, changed ABI alignment and changed destination object address.
  Section 9.3: integrate the existing approved f128, dynamic alloca, record
  varargs, atomic RMW, frame depth, relocation, declaration/variadic and call
  marker spellings. Repair ptr.offset and stale assembly-gap/volatile text.
  These are Appendix D integrations; no new source admission or canonical
  byte change. This does not assert the whole grammar is complete.

GREEN (existing target/frontend, two jobs, --locked --offline)
  cargo test -p evocc-evoir --test section9_completeness
    --test spec_grammar_contract: 5 PASS.
  cargo test -p evocc-proofcheck --test copy_is_opaque: 17 PASS,
    including the new positive replay and four semantic forgery rejections.
  tools/gate-changed.sh 703661d --locked --offline: exit 0,
    1644 PASS / 0 FAIL / 4 historical ignored, 211 result groups; eight crates.
  The final expanded sentinel was rerun after that gate, with both selected
    suites and all 17 checker tests; Clippy for both crates with --tests and
    -D warnings, cargo fmt --all -- --check, git diff --check all exit 0.
  tools/check-textual-grammar.py: 54/54 shapes, no differences. This heuristic
    is NOT evidence of complete grammar/semantic coverage.

